// Certified Public Accountant — the trickiest track in the catalog.
//
// Read src/data/tracks/CONTRACT.md before editing. CPA splits cleanly in two:
//   - the EXAM is national. One Uniform CPA Examination, written by the AICPA,
//     administered through NASBA, delivered at Prometric. That lives in globalSpec.
//   - the LICENSE is per-state. Fifty-one boards of accountancy, each with its own
//     education pathway, experience rule, ethics requirement, fee schedule and CPE
//     cycle. That lives in stateSpecs, where vendor/questions/time/pass are all "—"
//     because those fields describe an exam and this is licensure data.
//
// Two facts move constantly right now and are the ones aggregators get wrong:
//   1. The conditional-credit window. The old 18-month rule was replaced by a
//      30-month rule (NASBA UAA Model Rule 5-7, adopted April 21, 2023). Boards
//      adopted it on their own timetables. Every NASBA jurisdiction page checked in
//      2026 states 30 months — except Indiana, which publishes 36.
//   2. The 150-hour rule. Since the May 2025 UAA amendment, a majority of
//      jurisdictions have added a bachelor's-degree (120-hour) pathway paired with
//      two years of experience. Effective dates differ by state, some as late as 2027.
//
// 'unconfirmed' below means no primary source published the figure. Board licensure
// fees in particular are scattered across fee schedules, statutes and renewal portals;
// one widely-circulated aggregator table of "CPA renewal fees by state" was checked
// against California, New York, Virginia, Ohio and Washington and disagreed with the
// boards on all five, so nothing from it was used.

