  genericSpecNote: "Licensure requirements not yet verified for this jurisdiction. The EXAM is national and is fully specified above — 4 sections, 4 hours each, scaled 75 to pass, $268.59 per section. What varies here is the LICENSE. Typical ranges: 150 semester hours (or, in a growing majority of states since the May 2025 UAA amendment, a bachelor's degree plus two years of experience); one to two years of experience verified by a licensed CPA; an AICPA ethics course in most states, with California, Texas and Utah among those running their own state ethics or law exams; and 40 CPE hours per year or 80 per two years, ethics included. Confirm every figure with the state board of accountancy — aggregator fee tables were checked against five boards and disagreed with all five.",
